 Q. List all students older than 20
 -> SELECT * FROM students
    where age > 20;

 Q. Find the average score of each student.
 -> SELECT s.stud_id, s.stud_name, AVG(stud_score) AS average_score
    FROM students s
    JOINS marks m ON s.stud_id = m.stud_id
    GROUP BY s.stud_id,s.stud_name;

Q. Find the student with the highest total score.
-> SELECT stud_id, stud_name, SUM(m.stud_score) As total_score
   FROM students s
   JOINS marks m ON s.stud_id = m.stud_id
   GROUP BY s.stud_id, s.stud_name
   ORDER BY total_score DESC
   LIMIT 1;

Q. Find students who have no marks.
-> SELECT s.* FROM students s
   LEFT JOIN marks m ON s.stud_id = m.stud_id
   WHERE m.stud_id IS NULL;


Task 2: Design a small database schema for a Library Management System with: Books, Members, Loans tables
